# Keep local state and secrets out of the Docker build context.
# Without this, a stray node_modules/ inside vendor/moody-ai (e.g. from
# running an extension's tests locally) gets COPYed into the image and
# breaks the in-image `npm install` with arborist errors such as:
#   "Cannot destructure property 'package' of 'node.target' as it is null"

# Node — never bake host-installed trees into images (Dockerfiles run their own
# npm installs). NOTE: patterns are anchored to the context root, so nested
# trees (e.g. vendor/moody-ai/extensions/*/node_modules) need **/.
# A stray tree with dangling symlinks makes in-image `npm install` crash with:
#   "Cannot destructure property 'package' of 'node.target' as it is null"
**/node_modules/

# Local npm lockfiles inside the vendored moody-ai extensions (untracked local
# state; the Dockerfile installs fresh). The dq-made-easy-ui lockfile under
# docker/pi-dev-agent/repo-deps IS required by its `npm ci` step — keep it.
vendor/moody-ai/extensions/*/package-lock.json

# Git
.git/

# Local env files with secrets (loaded by build scripts on the host, not via COPY)
.env*.local

# Python / local scratch
venv/
venv.bak/
__pycache__/
tmp/

# Misc
*.log
.DS_Store
